## Data access with GORM

The store in `{{.Slots.store.Dir}}` uses [GORM](https://gorm.io/) on the
connection opened by `{{.Slots.database.Dir}}`. The tables are defined only in
`{{.Slots.database.Dir}}/{{index .Traits "sql-schema"}}`; the store does not
call `AutoMigrate`, so the schema file stays the single source of truth. When
you add a column, add it to the schema and to the struct in
`{{.Slots.store.Dir}}/store.go`.
{{- if eq (index .Traits "sql-dialect") "sqlite"}}

GORM talks to SQLite through
[github.com/libtnb/sqlite](https://github.com/libtnb/sqlite), a pure-Go dialect
on the same modernc.org/sqlite driver, so the project still builds without cgo.
{{- end}}
